  "steps": [
    "Tzatziki: grate the cucumber on the large holes of a box grater, then wring out the liquid in a kitchen towel.",
    "In a medium bowl, mix the cucumber, yogurt, lemon juice, dill, mint, garlic, olive oil and salt. Cover and refrigerate (keeps up to 3 days).",
    "Burgers: mix the meat with the onion, garlic, mint, salt, pepper, oregano and paprika until fully combined. Roll into 4 balls.",
    "Heat a flat-top griddle or cast iron pan over medium-high heat and oil it well.",
    "Set a meatball on the hot surface, lay a pita on top, and smash down hard with a heavy pan or burger press until as flat as you can get it.",
    "Cook 3-4 minutes, until the meat is crispy and cooked through (160°F). Flip and cook about 1 minute, until the pita is golden. Repeat with the rest.",
    "Top with lettuce, tomato, cucumber, red onion, feta, za'atar and tzatziki."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Smash the pita directly onto the meat so they fuse (the method @chilesandsmoke made viral).",
    "The blog version cooks 4-5 minutes before flipping; go longer if your patties are thicker.",
    "Instead of smashing a ball, you can spread the raw meat thinly over the pita and lay it meat side down."
  ],
